  "description": "SUGTEX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C120 H86 Nd4 O26 2-,2(C6 H16 N1 1+),3(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.769-4.035 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.41-113.27°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd4(O-DBM)4(HO-DBM)4(μ3-OH)2][Et3NH]2·3CH2Cl2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
